      "tag": "h1",
      "text": "The 4-Step Blueprint to Building a Profitable Private Practice"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "This FREE masterclass breaks it all down for you. You’ll learn a simple 4-step framework to start or grow your private practice with more confidence and less chaos. No guesswork. No overwhelm. No piecing together random advice."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "If you want clear direction, a smarter not harder strategy, and a roadmap that helps you avoid the common pitfalls new practice owners face, this masterclass is your first step."
    },
    {
      "tag": "button",
      "text": "WATCH FREE CLASS NOW!"
    },
    {
      "tag": "h1",
      "text": "MEET YVETTE"
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "I’m here to help therapists turn their clinical skills into sustainable, aligned businesses—without burning out or breaking their values."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Here, it’s not either/or. It’s impact and income. Ethics and ease. Purpose and profit."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "I didn’t start out wanting to be an entrepreneur—I started out trying to survive a broken system. I worked underpaid agency jobs, chased licensure, juggled multiple roles, and learned the hard way what school never taught us: being a great therapist doesn’t automatically build a great business."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "So I built my own."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "I grew from solo practitioner to group practice owner, made every mistake imaginable, navigated insurance chaos, scaled into a W2 agency, and learned how to lead a practice that supports both clients and clinicians. Today, I run a thriving group practice, serve as a clinical supervisor, and build businesses that create freedom, flexibility, and stability—for me and for the therapists I support."
    },
    {
      "tag": "p",
      "text": "Now, through Boss Clinician , I teach therapists how to become CEOs of their clinical expertise and build practices that actually support their lives."
    },
